---
/**
 * The shimmering placeholder a panel shows until its picture arrives.
 *
 * Deliberately not react-loading-skeleton's <Skeleton>: that one is a React
 * component, so it could not paint until the bundle had been fetched, parsed
 * and hydrated -- which on a slow connection is exactly when the placeholder
 * is wanted and exactly when it would not be there. This renders with the
 * HTML, before any script, and draws the same sweep in CSS.
 *
 * Placed *before* the image it stands in for: once the picture paints it
 * covers the skeleton on its own, without waiting to be told.
 */
---

<span class="skeleton" data-skeleton aria-hidden="true"></span>
